        <section id="how-to-take-wegovy-tablets">
          <h2>How to Take Wegovy Tablets</h2>
          <div class="tab-content-sec">
            <p>Wegovy tablets come in four strengths: 1.5mg, 4mg, 9mg, and 25mg. Treatment starts at the lowest dose and increases every 30 days, giving your body time to adjust and reducing the chance of side effects.</p>
            <h3>How to take each dose</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Take once every morning on an empty stomach</li>
              <li>Swallow whole with no more than 100ml of water — more than this reduces absorption</li>
              <li>Do not chew, split, or dissolve the tablet</li>
              <li>Wait at least 30 minutes before eating, drinking (anything other than water), or taking other medicines</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="switching-from-injection-to-tablet">
          <h2>Can I Switch From the Wegovy Injection to the Tablet?</h2>
          <div class="tab-content-sec">
            <p>Yes. Because the tablet and injection are absorbed differently, switching requires prescriber guidance rather than a straightforward dose-for-dose swap. The general approach is to restart the titration schedule from the lowest dose (1.5mg), with your prescriber advising on the most appropriate starting point for your circumstances.</p>
            <p><em>Please note: There is no officially published UK switching protocol. The guidance above is based on clinical principles only. Always consult your prescriber before making any changes to your treatment.</em></p>
            <p class="read-more-link content-description"><a href="https://www.pharmacyplanet.com/can-you-switch-to-wegovy-tablets-from-weight-loss-injections" style="color: #2C596D;
    font-weight: 600;">Read More</a></p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="who-is-eligible-for-wegovy-tablets">
          <h2>Who Is Eligible for Wegovy Tablets?</h2>
          <div class="tab-content-sec">
            <p>Wegovy tablets are prescribed for adults who meet at least one of the following criteria:</p>
            <h3>Standard eligibility</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>BMI of 30 or above, or</li>
              <li>BMI of 27 or above with a weight-related health condition (such as high blood pressure, high cholesterol, or type 2 diabetes)</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="read-more-link content-description"><a href="https://www.pharmacyplanet.com/what-are-the-eligibility-requirements-for-wegovy-tablets" style="color: #2C596D;
    font-weight: 600;">Read More</a></p>
            <h3>Minority ethnic backgrounds</h3>
            <p>Clinical guidelines recognise that people from certain minority ethnic groups carry a higher risk of weight-related conditions at a lower BMI. For these patients, the thresholds are:</p>
            <ul>
              <li>BMI of 27 or above, or</li>
              <li>BMI of 25 or above with a weight-related health condition</li>
            </ul>
            <p>A prescriber will assess your full medical history before treatment is approved.</p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="who-cannot-take-wegovy-tablets">
          <h2>Who Cannot Take Wegovy Tablets?</h2>
          <div class="tab-content-sec">
            <p>Wegovy tablets are not suitable for everyone. You should not take them if any of the following apply:</p>
            <h3>Medical conditions</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Personal or family history of medullary thyroid carcinoma (a type of thyroid cancer)</li>
              <li>Multiple Endocrine Neoplasia syndrome type 2 (MEN 2)</li>
              <li>History of pancreatitis</li>
              <li>Severe kidney or liver disease</li>
              <li>Diabetic retinopathy</li>
              <li>Severe gastrointestinal disease, including gastroparesis</li>
              <li>Allergy to semaglutide or any ingredient in the tablet</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Pregnancy and breastfeeding</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Pregnant, planning pregnancy, or breastfeeding</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Other medications</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Currently taking other GLP-1 medicines (Wegovy injections, Ozempic, Rybelsus)</li>
              <li>Taking insulin or certain diabetes medications (dose adjustments may be required under medical supervision)</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Age</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Under 18 years of age</li>
            </ul>
            <p>If you're unsure whether Wegovy tablets are suitable for you, our prescribers can assess your circumstances through a short online consultation.</p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="wegovy-tablets-side-effects">
          <h2>Side Effects of Wegovy Tablets</h2>
          <div class="tab-content-sec">
            <p>The most common side effects affect the digestive system and are usually most noticeable when starting treatment or moving to a higher dose. Gradual dose titration is specifically designed to reduce both the frequency and severity of these effects.</p>
            <p>Common side effects include nausea, diarrhoea, vomiting, constipation, and stomach discomfort. These are typically temporary and improve as your body adjusts to the medication.</p>
            <p>Contact your prescriber if side effects are persistent or severe. Full information is included in the patient information leaflet supplied with your medication.</p>
 <p class="read-more-link content-description"><a href="https://www.pharmacyplanet.com/side-effects-of-wegovy-tablets" style="color: #2C596D;
    font-weight: 600;">Read More</a></p>

          </div>
        </section>


        <section id="what-happens-wegovy-tablets">
          <h2>What Happens When You Stop Taking Wegovy Tablets?</h2>
          <div class="tab-content-sec">
            <p>Reaching your goal weight is a big milestone, and it’s natural to wonder what happens next. Once you stop taking Wegovy tablets, the appetite-reducing effect fades gradually rather than overnight, giving your body time to adjust. Weight regain isn’t inevitable; it largely depends on the habits you’ve built during treatment.</p>
            <p>Our clinical team can help you decide when to stop and support you afterwards so you can give yourself the best chance of maintaining your results.</p>
 <p class="read-more-link content-description"><a href="https://www.pharmacyplanet.com/what-happens-when-you-stop-taking-wegovy-tablets" style="color: #2C596D;
    font-weight: 600;">Read More</a></p>

          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="how-much-do-wegovy-tablets-cost">
          <h2>How Much Do Wegovy Tablets Cost?</h2>
          <div class="tab-content-sec">
            <p>Wegovy tablets are available from Pharmacy Planet from as low as £95 per month. Pricing is based on the dose prescribed, with costs typically increasing as you titrate through the schedule.</p>
            <p>There are no hidden consultation fees. Complete your online consultation and, if suitable, your prescription and medication are arranged through the same simple process.</p>
            <p class="read-more-link content-description"><a href="https://www.pharmacyplanet.com/how-much-do-wegovy-tablets-cost" style="color: #2C596D;
    font-weight: 600;">Read More</a></p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="wegovy-tablets-nhs">
          <h2>Are Wegovy Tablets Available on the NHS?</h2>
          <div class="tab-content-sec">
            <p>Wegovy tablets are not currently available on the NHS. If NICE recommends them in future, access would likely follow similar criteria to Wegovy injections — requiring referral through a specialist weight management service, strict BMI thresholds, and evidence that other weight loss approaches have already been tried.</p>
            <p>NHS waiting lists for these services are long, and many clinically eligible patients wait months or years. Private prescribing through Pharmacy Planet means no GP referral, no waiting list, and a consultation you can complete today.</p>

            <p class="read-more-link content-description"><a href="https://www.pharmacyplanet.com/can-you-switch-to-pharmacy-planet-from-another-provider" style="color: #2C596D;
    font-weight: 600;">Read More</a></p>
          </div>
        </section>


        <section id="what-makes-pharmacy-planet-wegovy-tablets">
          <h2>What Makes Pharmacy Planet the Right Choice for Wegovy Tablets?</h2>
          <div class="tab-content-sec">
            <p>A fair price is only part of the equation. Just as important is trusting that your prescription has been checked by a qualified clinician and knowing you can reach someone quickly if you need advice. At Pharmacy Planet, every prescription is reviewed by a UK-registered clinician, and our Lowest Price Guarantee means costs stay competitive throughout your journey, not just at the first order. There are no subscriptions or tie-ins, so you only order when you need to. If you have a question about your dose or how you're getting on, our team is reachable by phone, email or WhatsApp, so you're never left managing your treatment alone.</p>

            <p class="read-more-link content-description"><a href="https://www.pharmacyplanet.com/why-choose-pharmacy-planet-for-wegovy-tablets" style="color: #2C596D;
    font-weight: 600;">Read More</a></p>
          </div>
        </section>

