      <div class="faq-list">
        <button class="accordion-p">How to Take Wegovy Tablets</button>
        <div class="panel-p">
          <p>Wegovy tablets come in four strengths: 1.5mg, 4mg, 9mg, and 25mg. Treatment starts at the lowest dose and increases every 30 days, giving your body time to adjust and reducing the chance of side effects.</p>
          <h4>How to take each dose</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>Take once every morning on an empty stomach</li>
            <li>Swallow whole with no more than 100ml of water — more than this reduces absorption</li>
            <li>Do not chew, split, or dissolve the tablet</li>
            <li>Wait at least 30 minutes before eating, drinking (anything other than water), or taking other medicines</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-list">
        <button class="accordion-p">Can I Switch From the Wegovy Injection to the Tablet?</button>
        <div class="panel-p">
          <p>Yes. Because the tablet and injection are absorbed differently, switching requires prescriber guidance rather than a straightforward dose-for-dose swap. The general approach is to restart the titration schedule from the lowest dose (1.5mg), with your prescriber advising on the most appropriate starting point for your circumstances.</p>
          <p><em>Please note: There is no officially published UK switching protocol. The guidance above is based on clinical principles only. Always consult your prescriber before making any changes to your treatment.</em></p>
          <p class="read-more-link content-description"><a href="https://www.pharmacyplanet.com/can-you-switch-to-wegovy-tablets-from-weight-loss-injections" style="color: #2C596D;
    font-weight: 600;">Read More</a></p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-list">
        <button class="accordion-p">Who Is Eligible for Wegovy Tablets?</button>
        <div class="panel-p">
          <p>Wegovy tablets are prescribed for adults who meet at least one of the following criteria:</p>
          <h4>Standard eligibility</h4>
          <ul>
              <li>BMI of 30 or above, or</li>
              <li>BMI of 27 or above with a weight-related health condition (such as high blood pressure, high cholesterol, or type 2 diabetes)</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="read-more-link content-description"><a href="https://www.pharmacyplanet.com/what-are-the-eligibility-requirements-for-wegovy-tablets" style="color: #2C596D;
    font-weight: 600;">Read More</a></p>
            <h3>Minority ethnic backgrounds</h3>
            <p>Clinical guidelines recognise that people from certain minority ethnic groups carry a higher risk of weight-related conditions at a lower BMI. For these patients, the thresholds are:</p>
            <ul>
              <li>BMI of 27 or above, or</li>
              <li>BMI of 25 or above with a weight-related health condition</li>
            </ul>
            <p>A prescriber will assess your full medical history before treatment is approved.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-list">
        <button class="accordion-p">Who Cannot Take Wegovy Tablets?</button>
        <div class="panel-p">
          <p><strong>Wegovy tablets are not suitable for everyone. You should not take them if any of the following apply:</strong></p>
          <h4>Medical conditions</h4>
            <ul>
              <li>Personal or family history of medullary thyroid carcinoma (a type of thyroid cancer)</li>
              <li>Multiple Endocrine Neoplasia syndrome type 2 (MEN 2)</li>
              <li>History of pancreatitis</li>
              <li>Severe kidney or liver disease</li>
              <li>Diabetic retinopathy</li>
              <li>Severe gastrointestinal disease, including gastroparesis</li>
              <li>Allergy to semaglutide or any ingredient in the tablet</li>
            </ul>
            <h4>Pregnancy and breastfeeding</h4>
            <ul>
              <li>Pregnant, planning pregnancy, or breastfeeding</li>
            </ul>
            <h4>Other medications</h4>
            <ul>
              <li>Currently taking other GLP-1 medicines (Wegovy injections, Ozempic, Rybelsus)</li>
              <li>Taking insulin or certain diabetes medications (dose adjustments may be required under medical supervision)</li>
            </ul>
            <h4>Age</h4>
            <ul>
              <li>Under 18 years of age</li>
            </ul>
            <p>If you're unsure whether Wegovy tablets are suitable for you, our prescribers can assess your circumstances through a short online consultation.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-list">
        <button class="accordion-p">Side Effects of Wegovy Tablets</button>
        <div class="panel-p">
          <p>The most common side effects affect the digestive system and are usually most noticeable when starting treatment or moving to a higher dose. Gradual dose titration is specifically designed to reduce both the frequency and severity of these effects.</p>
          <p>Common side effects include nausea, diarrhoea, vomiting, constipation, and stomach discomfort. These are typically temporary and improve as your body adjusts to the medication.</p>
          <p>Contact your prescriber if side effects are persistent or severe. Full information is included in the patient information leaflet supplied with your medication.</p>
